  <p><strong>Effective 24 August 2026.</strong></p>
  <h2>Use and safety</h2>
  <p>Chef assists with meal planning, recipes, nutrition estimates and grocery preparation. Check all ingredients, allergens, dietary suitability, nutrition, quantities, prices, product availability and current product labels yourself.</p>
  <p>Chef is not medical, nutritional, allergy or dietetic advice. Generated output must never be the only safety check. Confirm safety needs with the affected person and seek appropriate professional advice when needed.</p>

  <h2>Optional Computer Use</h2>
  <p>A request for a grocery list does not authorise a live basket change. When a user directly asks Chef to fill or change a cart, basket or trolley, Chef may use an available browser or shopping capability to prepare it. No separate token is required.</p>
  <p>Checkout, payment, fulfilment, address changes, restricted products and order placement are outside Chef's scope and remain human-controlled.</p>
  <p>Chef is independent software. It is not sponsored, endorsed or approved by Coles, Woolworths or any other retailer. Users are responsible for complying with each provider's terms and applicable law.</p>

  <h2>Local and session-only memory</h2>
  <p>Durable Markdown memory is available only on hosts with appropriate local file access. Other hosts may retain context only for the current session or under their own memory features. Users are responsible for protecting and backing up local files.</p>

  <h2>Licence and warranty</h2>
  <p>The source is available under the MIT Licence and is provided without warranty to the maximum extent permitted by law. Nothing here excludes rights that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
